A HEAD request for a file is passed to send_file_and_exit with only
SEND_HEADERS, but nothing there checked SEND_BODY, so the file's
contents followed the headers anyway, as for GET. A HEAD with a Range
header also got the body, since the range code replaced "what" with
SEND_BODY after sending the 206 headers.

Stop after the headers when SEND_BODY is not set, and have the range
code only clear SEND_HEADERS.

---
 networking/httpd.c |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/networking/httpd.c
+++ b/networking/httpd.c
@@ -2148,12 +2148,14 @@
 		} else {
 			range_len = range_end - range_start + 1;
 			send_headers(HTTP_PARTIAL_CONTENT);
-			what = SEND_BODY;
+			what &= ~SEND_HEADERS;
 		}
 	}
 #endif
 	if (what & SEND_HEADERS)
 		send_headers(HTTP_OK);
+	if (!(what & SEND_BODY))
+		send_EOF_and_exit();
 
 	/* Sending BODY */
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_USE_SENDFILE
